WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.120
What it do, what it do?

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:23.320
This week on Thug Notes, we hittin dat true-blue sea with "Life of Pi" by Yann Martel.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.700
Da book start with a shady first section called “Author’s Note,"

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.220
where a nameless narrator flexin like he the author of this book.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:35.960
Brotha jus chillin, sippin on coffee, when he start choppin it up with a hood named Francis.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:42.460
Now dis geezer all like, “Say dawg, I bet I can tell you a story dat’s so tight, it's gonna make you believe in God!”

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.920
“Oh, sh*t. I gotta hear dis, man!”

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.080
Francis start yappin bout a boy named Pi he knew back in the day.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:55.500
Pi’s story is so damn trill, da narrator gotta hit up Pi, himself, to get the legit story.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.520
It go a lil somethin like this:

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:01.080
As a lil boy, Pi was comin up in Pondicherry, India,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.620
where his parents runnin a zoo that gave em enough cash flow to live a pretty cush lifestyle.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:12.000
Oh, and real quick — “Pi” ain’t this lil thug’s full name — it’s Piscine Molitor Patel.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.160
But since erryone always on his nuts callin him names like “Pissing,”

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.160
he decide “Pi” gonna be his new street name.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:23.600
Now Pi was actually raised a Hindu, and he is all about dat jam.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.640
Still, it don’t stop his fourteen-year-old self from sniffin around Christianity and Islam.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.100
Eventually, he decide he gonna rep all three religions —

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.900
even though his parents, and the local holy rollers, ain’t feelin it.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:43.480
But Pi ain’t trippin. Cuz to him, all religions are true, and he just wanna show love to da man upstairs.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:48.280
And it’s a good thing Pi so open-minded,
cuz his little ass bout to move cross da world.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.760
Since Pi’s mom and pop ain’t down with some political sh*t happening in New India,

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.240
they decide to sell the zoo and peace out to Canada.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:02.720
So Pi, his fam, and all their animal homies hop up on a big-ass ship and start cruisin.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:08.080
But afta a couple days, a storm rages through da water and da ship starts sinkin.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.960
Pi-Dawg is da only member of his family to survive. Damn.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:18.460
Dude hops up on a lifeboat, but brotha gotta share it with an orangutan named OJ,

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.480
a zebra with a jacked-up leg, and a spotted hyena,

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.600
who start actin like a real d*ck when he decide to eat the other two animals.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:29.380
So not chill, spotted hyena. So not chill, man.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:34.560
But sh*t get even less chill when a 450-pound tiger, named Richard Parker,

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.000
pop up from under a tarp and merc dat hater.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:45.200
Pi like, “Man, f**k this.” So he ghetto-rig himself a raft to keep his distance from Richie P’s crazy self.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.400
Pi finally recognize dat the raft ain’t gonna be enough to save his ass;

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:54.900
da only way he gonna survive dis mess is by puttin dat tiger in check with some training.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.780
Pi straight alpha males dat b*tch.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.400
With da help of survival guides, some rations,

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:04.820
and other supplies — Pi able to survive in
da Pacific Ocean for a long-ass time.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:11.820
Dat don’t mean it’s easy, though. At one point, Pi get so dehydrated that he goes blind and his mind start slippin.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:16.300
Matta fact, he goin so damn crazy that he start conversatin wit Richard Parker

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.620
bout their favorite kind of munchies.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:23.640
Turns out, Pi wasn’t talkin to Richard at
all — instead, it was another blind castaway:

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.180
this French fool, who float up, and Pi like,

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:31.220
"Ma man! Hop up on this here life raft, and get yoself some rest, dawg!"

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.820
But when the dude try to boot up and merc Pi, Richard Parker like,

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.800
“B*tch nuh-uh!" and rips dat sucka up.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:38.760
He dead.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:43.480
Later, Pi’s boat lands on an island dat survives by eatin brothas.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.180
Yeah — you heard dat right.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.600
Pi just about loses his sh*t when he finds teeth inside a piece of fruit.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:50.660
Ugggh!

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:53.700
So Pi and Richard Parker chunk deuces outta dat trap.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:04:00.960
After over 200 days on da struggle, in dat watery abyss, their lifeboat washes up on to the shore of Mexico,

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:06.040
and Richard Parker rolls out in to da jungle without even saying bye or nothin.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.560
What a d*ck, man.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.100
Pi gets picked up, taken to a hospital,

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:14.780
and later questioned by two dudes from the Japanese Ministry of Transport.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.580
Pi tell em what went down, but these dudes like,

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:20.660
"Psh, this boy musta lost his damn mind.”

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:26.060
So Pi like, “Alright, alright. That too crazy for ya? You want somethin real? Check this out."

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:31.880
And he tell the story again, this time layin it down raw. He say he wasn’t on the boat with no animals.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:36.840
Instead, it was the ship’s cook, a sailor with a broken leg, and Pi’s own mama.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:41.980
Just like dat hyena, the cook iced both the sailor and Pi’s mama.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:47.460
But since Pi don’t play, he shanked dat
boy in the stomach, and then feasted on his corpse.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.120
Damn, Pi! You gangsta, dawg!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:55.760
But since neither story can be really proven, Pi just like, “Forget truth. Lemme ask you:

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.060
which story you like better?”

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.960
They like, “Eh, we’ll go with the animals one.”

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:09.420
Pi say, “Yeah? Well, just so you know, believing in God is the same exact jam.”

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:15.220
Now the title of this book ain’t just talkin bout the life of some dude named Pi — there’s more to it, playa.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:17.580
Just look at what Pi say about his name:

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:24.140
"...in that Greek letter that looks like a shack with a corrugated tin roof, in that elusive, irrational number

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.720
with which scientists try to understand the universe, I found refuge."

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:33.700
Pi see his name as a symbol for home — dat practical safety from da outside world.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.760
But at the same time, the number “pi” is irrational —

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:41.900
Cain’t nobody can make total sense of it, cuz it never terminates or has fixed boundaries.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.740
And that’s exactly what da book saying about all life:

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:49.020
it's a mix between da rational — things we can make sense of through science and reason —

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:53.460
and the irrational — things dat ain’t even da smartest hood on da block can figure out.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:55.660
Life of Pi — get it?

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:59.600
Now don’t get me wrong: science, reason,
logic — dank.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:05.720
But dat don’t mean errything in life gotta be rational — da world gotta have a lil taste of madness, too.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:12.240
"All living things contain a measure of madness that moves them in strange, sometimes inexplicable ways.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:20.400
This madness can be saving; it is part and parcel of the ability to adapt. Without it, no species would survive."

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.760
When da sh*t hits the fan, it’s religion — the non-rational element —

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:28.900
that gives Pi the juice to survive and make sense of da world around him.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:34.380
"Yes, so long as God is with me, I will not die. Amen..."

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:38.880
Pi might have dat religion game on lock, but it don’t mean dat he’s got all da answers.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:45.220
Ain’t no doubt dat P-dawg gets sh*t on, in the novel, and has trouble comin to terms with all his sufferin.

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:51.700
So one one hand, Pi realize dat da mess he go through up on dat raft don’t mean a damn thing to the universe.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:55.960
But on the other hand — to him — there ain’t nothin more important.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:57.640
Cuz it’s all he knows.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:03.000
In a cold, dark universe, not only is your suffering relative, but truth is too.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.060
All throughout this book we gettin muddied representations of what’s real.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:11.000
I mean, who is this fool callin himself the “author” at the beginning?

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:17.660
And at the end, Pi pretty much tell us that the whole story bout him and Richard Parker could all be bunk.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:24.340
Hell, there’s a good reason to believe dat Richard Parker is jus the savage, kill-or-be-killed side of Pi.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:28.900
Peep da subtle ways dat lil thug and Richie P associated with each other.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:33.800
"Since we are on the subject, I became as constipated as Richard Parker."

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:38.760
"I began to imitate Richard Parker in sleeping an incredible number of hours."

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:45.460
But who da hell knows? I guess the realest truth is there ain’t no way to tell what really went down on dat raft.

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:49.860
Hell, both of da stories Pi lay on us might be total bullsh*t.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:53.340
So like Pi say, does it really matter what’s
actually true?

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:55.960
Should we just go wit what’s better for us?

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:02.940
Sure rationality and practicality are worth fighting for, but maybe it ain’t always so important to know the real deal.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:07.580
Maybe the best thing is just goin with what’s gonna help you cope and give you hope.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:08.660
Naw mean?

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:11.260
Ay, thanks for watching ma well read ballas.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.140
Peace!

